# S3.2 — cloud sync build configuration. Copy to `berilo.properties` (gitignored)
# and fill in. Absent or blank, the app still builds and runs; the account/sync
# surface is disabled behind a stated message instead.
#
# Both values are PUBLIC client configuration, not secrets:
#   - the Clerk publishable key is the same string the web app ships in its JS
#     bundle; it identifies the Clerk instance and authorizes nothing on its own,
#   - the base URL is the published API host.
# They are kept out of git so this repository stays free of environment-specific
# values. The secret half of the pair — CLERK_SECRET_KEY, SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY —
# belongs only to `berilo-cloud` and must never reach the app: the client holds a
# short-lived Clerk session JWT, and Postgres RLS is what actually enforces
# isolation (docs/sync_api.md §1.1).
#
# CI/release builds may instead export BERILO_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY and
# BERILO_API_BASE_URL; berilo.properties wins when both are present.

# From https://dashboard.clerk.com -> API keys (pk_test_... in dev, pk_live_... in prod).
clerkPublishableKey=pk_test_...

# Defaults to https://berilo.app/api/v1 when unset. Point at a local Next.js dev
# server (e.g. http://10.0.2.2:3000/api/v1 from the emulator) to sync against it.
apiBaseUrl=https://berilo.app/api/v1
